@api = http://localhost:3333

### Ping — the scaffold route, no auth, no database
GET {{api}}/

### CSRF token
# The front reads the XSRF-TOKEN cookie; a scripted client cannot decrypt it,
# so it reads the raw token here instead. Development and test only.
# @name csrf
GET {{api}}/api/v1/auth/csrf

@csrfToken = {{csrf.response.body.csrfToken}}

### Login — sets the session cookie, kept by the REST client for later requests
POST {{api}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "email": "player@wanderlore.test", "password": "password" }

### Profile
GET {{api}}/api/v1/account/profile

### Mes parties
GET {{api}}/api/v1/sessions

### Tour de jeu
@sid = 1a8ccf4d-7d06-4b22-a463-b9ab8c7bef2c

# Une clé neuve par soumission. La figer pour rejouer la même requête : le
# backend renvoie alors le tour déjà enregistré, sans rappeler le LLM.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sid}}/turns
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "playerInput": "I look around me" }

### Vue d'une partie
GET {{api}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sid}}

### Historique des tours aboutis
GET {{api}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sid}}/turns

### Lecture d'un tour (rattrapage) — id pris dans l'historique
@turnId = a68faff5-e621-4126-add0-f5a223001b61
GET {{api}}/api/v1/sessions/{{sid}}/turns/{{turnId}}

### Logout
POST {{api}}/api/v1/account/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
